<title>ITALY: Turin busiest Italian airport in '96 for cargo charters.</title>
<headline>Turin busiest Italian airport in '96 for cargo charters.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turin was the busiest Italian airport for cargo charters in 1996 accounting for nearly 28 percent of all Italian cargo charters at 477 such flights against 209 in 1995, statistics published by Italy's civil aviation authority (Civilavia) show..</p>
<p>This was in sharp contrast to 1995 when figures were distorted by a large number of small Piper PA-31 charters carrying computer parts from Catania in Scily to Malta.</p>
<p>In 1995 the Catania flights totalled 523 out of the total flights of 1,729 making it the busiest airport for cargo charters in terms of flights flown.</p>
